<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sanctuary of Fortuna Primigenia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sanctuary of Fortuna Primigenia was a great temple complex of the goddess Fortuna at Praeneste, modern Palestrina, east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. It was famous for an oracle in which lots were drawn, and in the late 2nd century BCE it was rebuilt as a series of monumental terraces climbing the hillside, one of the largest religious complexes of Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sanctuary-of-fortuna-primigenia.jpg" alt="Sanctuary of Fortuna Primigenia" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Camelia.boban · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sanctuary_of_Fortuna_Primigenia_30.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
